Package: recm
Type: Package
Title: Rational Error Correction Model
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      given = "LJ",
      family = "Valencia",
      email = "leb_valencia@yahoo.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: Estimation of polynomial adjustment cost (PAC) equations under a
    rational error correction (REC) framework, the forward-looking
    error-correction specification used in the Federal Reserve Board's FRB/US
    model and the Bank of Canada's LENS model. Given a decision variable, a
    frictionless target and a calibrated discount factor, the package recovers
    the adjustment cost parameters and reports the implied decision rule in
    both the explicit and the compressed (LENS-style) formats. Because the
    criterion is routinely near-flat, profile and bootstrap diagnostics are
    treated as part of the standard output rather than as optional extras.
